  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$(-2)^{7}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that $-2=(-1)\\times 2.$\n\nTo raise the product of two numbers to the power of $7$, we can raise each number to the power of $7,$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n(-2)^{7}={((-1)\\times 2)}^{7}=(-1)^{7}\\times {2}^{7}\n$$\n\nSince $-1$ raised to an odd power is $-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n(-1)^{7}\\times {2}^{7}=(-1)\\times {2}^{7}=-{2}^{7}.\n$$",
